body: "Reproduced against `3c1f8cab89d851d9dc4cc8e5da86d8ac8874e3d0` (fetched main), Node 24.19.0, with the repository lockfile and SDK 2026.11.4. Only synthetic input and temporary local trackers were used.\n\nThe secret guard rejects `password=SyntheticOnly123!` but accepts `{\"password\":\"SyntheticOnly123!\"}`. The latter is stored as durable memory and copied into an agents-md export.\n\nSource:\n- [The assignment matcher permits whitespace, but no closing quote, between the credential key and its separator](https://github.com/unbraind/pm-memory/blob/3c1f8cab89d851d9dc4cc8e5da86d8ac8874e3d0/src/core.ts#L40-L49).\n- [remember calls this guard before persistence](https://github.com/unbraind/pm-memory/blob/3c1f8cab89d851d9dc4cc8e5da86d8ac8874e3d0/src/memory.ts#L16-L24).\n\nReproduction:\n\n```sh\nreview=$(mktemp -d)\ngit clone --quiet https://github.com/unbraind/pm-memory.git \"$review/package\"\ncd \"$review/package\"\ngit checkout --quiet 3c1f8cab89d851d9dc4cc8e5da86d8ac8874e3d0\nnpm ci --ignore-scripts --no-audit --no-fund\nnpm run build\ncat > repro-secret.mjs <<'JS'\nimport assert from 'node:assert/strict';\nimport { mkdtemp, readFile, readdir } from 'node:fs/promises';\nimport { tmpdir } from 'node:os';\nimport { join } from 'node:path';\nimport { PmClient } from '@unbrained/pm-cli/sdk';\nimport { remember, get, exportDir } from './dist/index.js';\nconst root = await mkdtemp(join(tmpdir(), 'memory-review-'));\nconst workspace = join(root, 'tracker');\nconst pm = new PmClient({ cwd: root, pmRoot: workspace, author: 'fixture', noExtensions: true });\nawait pm.init('fixture', { defaults: true, agentGuidance: 'skip', mergeFence: false });\nawait pm.config('project', 'set', 'agent_identity.probes_enabled', 'false');\nconst options = { workspace, author: 'fixture', kind: 'reference' };\ntry { await remember('password=SyntheticOnly123!', { ...options, slug: 'plain' }); console.log('plain=accepted'); }\ncatch (e) { assert.equal(e.code, 'privacy'); console.log('plain=privacy'); }\nconst fact = '{\"password\":\"SyntheticOnly123!\"}';\nawait remember(fact, { ...options, slug: 'quoted' });\nconst saved = await get('quoted', options);\nassert.equal(saved.body, fact);\nconsole.log('quoted=accepted; stored_verbatim=true');\nawait exportDir(join(root, 'export'), { workspace, author: 'fixture', to: 'agents-md' });\nasync function allText(dir) { let value = ''; for (const e of await readdir(dir, { withFileTypes: true })) value += e.isDirectory() ? await allText(join(dir, e.name)) : await readFile(join(dir, e.name), 'utf8'); return value; }\nconst exported = await allText(join(root, 'export'));\nconsole.log('export_contains_literal=' + exported.includes('SyntheticOnly123!'));\nJS\nnode repro-secret.mjs\n```\n\nObserved output:\n\n```text\nplain=privacy\nquoted=accepted; stored_verbatim=true\nexport_contains_literal=true\n```\n\nExpected: quoted JSON credential assignments receive the same typed privacy refusal as equivalent unquoted assignments, before any item/history write.\n\nActual: the quote after the key prevents the assignment expression from matching; ordinary passwords without a provider-specific token prefix pass every remaining check. The public SDK accepts and persists the entire JSON string.\n\nImpact: copied JSON configuration or API payloads can bypass the advertised credential refusal and carry secrets into durable history and portable agent context. The reproduction uses an intentionally synthetic password, not a live credential. This is independent of SDK admission/adoption work.\n\nSuggested direction: cover quoted credential keys in the bounded scanner, or inspect bounded structured input without losing the free-text guard. Add positive refusal controls for JSON and quoted YAML keys, including password and api_key, and verify no durable write occurs. Keep accepted secret-manager/environment references as explicit negative controls.\n\nDuplicate check: searched all issue states for privacy, secret, quoted, and password; no matching issue was found."
